    "result_text": "All tests pass (the suite contains the single `AcceptanceTest` class, which is green). The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec: *when more than 80 owners have already been created today, the response includes `bulkSignupWarning: true`, otherwise `false`.*\n\nI followed the codebase's existing pattern for derived owner fields (like `namesakeCount`, `customerCode`): compute at create time, persist on the entity, and expose it through the generated DTO so it's returned by both `POST /api/owners` and `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **New pipeline step** \u2014 `FlagBulkSignup.java`. Counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals the request's resolved business-day date (the same bucket `CheckDailyOwnerLimit` uses) and sets `bulkSignupWarning = count > 80` on the built owner. It runs before `SaveOwner`, so the new owner isn't self-counted \u2014 matching the \"already been created\" wording.\n\n2. **Wiring** \u2014 inserted a `bulkSignup` step into `owners.POST.yml` between `namesakes` and `save`, under `govern: [ transaction ]`.\n\n3. **Entity** \u2014 added the `bulkSignupWarning` (`Boolean`, column `bulk_signup_warning`) field with getter/setter to `Owner`.\n\n4. **Schema** \u2014 added `bulk_signup_warning BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE` to all four DB schemas (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres). The `DEFAULT FALSE` keeps pre-existing/seed rows non-null so GET always yields `false` when unset.\n\n5. **API contract** \u2014 added the `bulkSignupWarning` boolean (readOnly) property to the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml`; the generated `OwnerDto` picks it up and MapStruct maps it automatically (name matches the entity getter).\n\nThe threshold is 80 (warning at 81+ existing today), sitting below the existing daily limit of 100, so the warning and rejection ranges are consistent.",
